[2.0] Manu&Prod debug does not grant DMI register access #1129

Caliptra DMI registers are not accessible in Manuf debug and Prod debug security states.

Note: Credit to Nuvoton team for finding this
The Caliptra Core JTAG remains locked because the unlock_caliptra_security_state register stays asserted. This causes cptra_security_state_Latched_d.debug_locked and
cptra_security_state_Latched_f.debug_locked to never reach the required state of both being 0. As a result, the Caliptra Core JTAG cannot be released.

PR Title: [RTL] Fix for security state debug not unlocking after manuf/prod dbg unlock flow patch_v2.1
PR Number: #1132
Status: Merged (November 22, 2025)

Description:
The pull request addresses a bug in the security state capturing logic. According to the author, the change "removes the else condition from the second flop in the security state capturing logic." The static unlock signal was preventing the second register from receiving updated values after completing the debug unlock procedure.

Key Changes:
The submission consisted of three commits:
1. c724a52 - Removed the else term to allow the secondary flop to receive the updated value when manufacturing or production debug unlock is granted
2. 9e92dc5 - Fixed security state capturing flops for lint by properly observing the reset term
3. a7d582c - Automated pipeline timestamp and hash update following successful execution

